    "updated": "September 28, 2026",
    "body": "## Money or identity information at risk\n\nContact the payment provider or financial institution immediately. LotSocial cannot reverse a payment, recover an account, or replace an official fraud report. Use the [Fraud Awareness steps](/legal/fraud-awareness) and the official reporting channels listed there.\n\n## Preserve the evidence\n\n- The full URL of the social post or page where you saw it.\n- The dealership vehicle-page URL, if shown.\n- Vehicle year, make, model, VIN, or stock number when available.\n- A screenshot showing the issue, date, time, account name, and caption.\n- A short explanation of what appears wrong and how you verified it.\n- A safe contact method for follow-up. Do not include passwords, one-time codes, bank details, or unnecessary identity documents.\n\n## Use a verified channel\n\nIf you are a LotSocial pilot user, use the verified business or support channel that issued your access. If you are a consumer, contact the dealership through the main phone number or contact page on its official website and ask it to preserve the post and current vehicle record. Do not trust a contact method supplied only by the questioned social account.\n\nLotSocial does not publish an unverified reporting address in this v0.9 policy. That avoids directing sensitive reports to a guessed or impersonated destination.\n\n## Report format\n\nInclude the post or page URL, dealership vehicle URL, vehicle identifiers, issue type, what appears wrong, how you verified it, the observation date and time, and a safe method for follow-up.\n\n## What the recipient should do\n\nThe recipient should preserve the report, compare the post with the captured source and current dealership page, check the authorization record, and pause or correct affected content when warranted. A report does not promise a particular outcome or response time.\n\nSuspected fraud can also be reported at [ReportFraud.ftc.gov](https://reportfraud.ftc.gov/). Identity theft can be reported at [IdentityTheft.gov](https://www.identitytheft.gov/)."
