    "termsVersion": "2026-09-28-v0.9",
    "body": "## Agreement and pilot status\n\nThese terms apply to the LotSocial pilot. By accessing or using the pilot, you agree to follow these terms and the policies linked in the Legal Center. This is a pilot legal version under counsel review. A later version may replace it after review.\n\n## Authorized dealership use\n\nYou may use LotSocial only for lawful dealership marketing work that you are authorized to perform. You must have authority to market the vehicle and to use the facts, images, descriptions, feeds, and accounts involved.\n\n- Do not bypass a login, paywall, access control, robots restriction, or other technical safeguard.\n- Do not use manager approval as a substitute for rights controlled by a feed, media, or website provider.\n- Do not treat content creation or rendering as permission to publish to a dealership or social account.\n- Stop using material when permission is suspended, revoked, disputed, or expired.\n\n## Vehicle information and generated content\n\nLotSocial may read a public dealership vehicle-detail page and preserve source evidence from the time of import. Dealer pages can change and can contain errors. Automated extraction and AI-assisted copy can also be incomplete or wrong.\n\nBefore publishing, you must review the current source page and confirm the vehicle identity, availability, total advertised price, mandatory fees, incentive eligibility, equipment, images, disclosures, and every material claim. Do not publish or leave live content that you know is inaccurate.\n\nRead the [Listing Accuracy policy](/legal/accuracy) for the required verification standard.\n\n## LotSocial is not the seller\n\nLotSocial is a content and authorization tool. It does not own, sell, price, inspect, finance, guarantee, title, deliver, or accept deposits for vehicles. A dealership or salesperson remains responsible for the vehicle offer and the content they approve or publish.\n\n## Acceptable use\n\nDo not use LotSocial for deceptive, fraudulent, infringing, harassing, abusive, unlawful, or unauthorized activity. Do not introduce malicious code, probe for access, interfere with the service, impersonate another person or dealership, or use generated content to conceal a material fact.\n\n## User content and service operation\n\nYou keep whatever rights you already hold in material you submit. You permit LotSocial to process, store, transform, and display that material only as needed to operate, secure, troubleshoot, and improve the pilot and to produce the output you request.\n\nLotSocial may use hosting, storage, database, email, public-page retrieval, AI, and media-rendering providers to operate the pilot. Third-party services may have their own terms and availability limits.\n\n## Availability and changes\n\nThe pilot may change, experience interruptions, or contain defects. Features may be limited, suspended, or withdrawn. These terms and related policies may be updated by publishing a new version and effective date in the Legal Center.\n\n## Responsibility and remedies\n\nYou remain responsible for content you approve or publish, including dealership policy, advertising rules, intellectual-property rights, platform requirements, and applicable law. If a post is inaccurate, unauthorized, misleading, or suspicious, stop using it, preserve the evidence, and follow the [reporting process](/legal/report).\n\nTo the extent permitted by law, the pilot is provided without a promise that it will be uninterrupted, error-free, or suitable for every use. Counsel will review warranty, liability, governing-law, and dispute language before broader commercial release; this v0.9 pilot version does not add an arbitration or forum-selection clause."
